# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# Google Drive "load from link" support. Optional — with this unset the app
# still loads files from disk and from any CORS-enabled direct URL, and the
# Drive tab is hidden.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE SETTING IT:
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the built JavaScript. This key is
# therefore PUBLIC in any deployment and cannot be hidden. Keeping it out of
# git is hygiene, not a security boundary.
#
# The actual protection is restricting the key in Google Cloud Console:
#   1. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "Google Drive API"
#   2. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key
#   3. Edit the key:
#      - API restrictions:         restrict to "Google Drive API" only
#      - Application restrictions: "Websites", and list exactly the origins
#                                  you deploy to (plus http://localhost:5173
#                                  for local dev)
#
# With both restrictions in place a leaked key can only do what the app already
# does: read files that are already shared publicly, from your own origins.
#
# Only files shared as "Anyone with the link" can be read this way. Private
# files need OAuth + the Google Picker, which is not implemented.
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
